Viewer: a swipe is not ended by a lost pointer capture (2026-10-23).

On the car's browser the receiver saw finger down to up in 6-80 ms while the finger was still swiping, so
the phone took the gesture as a tap. A lost pointer capture no longer ends the touch (only pointerup and
pointercancel do), and a swipe that moved sends its final point as a move before the up, so an
animation-frame flush starved by decoding cannot turn the swipe into a single up at the end.

